From: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: support the 5K panel of the iMacPro1,1

The iMacPro1,1 drives its 5K panel like the iMac20,x, as two 2560x2880
tiles on an eDP root link and a DP tile link. Add it to the 5K quirk.

Signed-off-by: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
---
  drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_quirks.c | 7 +++++++
  1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_quirks.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_quirks.c
index 8657dd9..a34a455 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_quirks.c
@@ -173,6 +173,13 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id dmi_quirk_table[] = {
 			DMI_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "iMac20,2"),
 		},
 	},
+	{
+		.callback = imac5K_support_callback,
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "Apple Inc."),
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "iMacPro1,1"),
+		},
+	},
 	{}
 	/* TODO: refactor this from a fixed table to a dynamic option */
 };
